      "stop_reason": "end_turn",
      "tool_uses": [],
      "assistant_text": "The **Guarded Write Journal** page describes a mechanism for achieving all-or-nothing semantics for file writes. Here\u0027s what it covers:\n\nAccording to [[write-journal]], before the guarded tool executor overwrites any file, it records that file\u0027s prior state in an in-memory write journal. This means:\n\n- **Prior state recording**: The journal captures either the file\u0027s previous content (if it existed) or notes that it didn\u0027t exist.\n- **Rollback on failure**: If the agent run fails\u2014whether due to a turn cap, an unrecoverable error, or denied writes\u2014the journal can roll back all recorded writes in reverse order.\n- **Rollback details**: Files that previously existed are restored to their prior content, and newly created files are deleted.\n- **Transaction semantics**: This provides all-or-nothing semantics without needing a database\u2014the in-memory journal itself serves as the transaction log for a single run.\n\nThe page also notes that the Query agent never uses the journal\u0027s rollback path, since it has no write tool of its own\u2014only agents that actually write populate the journal.",
      "input_tokens": 5334,
      "output_tokens": 246
    }
